        {
          "id": 2141493183,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, it's a kind of little-endian notation and we have the highest in the stack on the left.\n\nOne note I left in the code, one day there could be another key below Interface (for example the original capture file if we merged several captures, or the capturing device name when dealing with multiple taps which don't have interface IDs). Although I am not sure such thing will happen.\n\nSecond note, with the V letter at the beginning and not at the end, I thought it was easier to pronounce something like \"veemay\" then \"yiamvvv\" if someone has to talk about this preference one day.\n\nMarking this as ready.\nAnd Thanks again for the feedback.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
